# React Loading State Patterns for Visual Stability

## Overview
Proper loading state management prevents layout shifts and improves user experience.

## Pattern 1: Skeleton Screens

Replace loading spinners/text with skeletons matching content dimensions.

```tsx
function ProductList() {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  // Show skeletons during loading
  if (loading) {
    return (
      <div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        {Array(6).fill(0).map((_, i) => (
